{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdgxPgqrnWEX2c5K1xad","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The candidate passed the admission self-check: it printed `OK`. A short test fit gave ELPD-LOO −3460.6, against −3465.7 for the current best model. That fit was only 100 draws on one chain, so the number is a rough guide, not a result.\n\n**Name:** `longest_repeated_chunk_aversion`\n\n**Hypothesis:** People look for the single most striking repeated chunk in a sequence. This is the longest stretch of flips that appears again, unchanged and not overlapping itself, somewhere else in the same sequence (HTT in HTTHHTTH, HTHT in HTHTHTHT). One long recurring chunk makes the sequence look copied and so less random. As the brief asked, the cue is a maximum over sub-sequences: one striking stretch decides it, not an average over the whole sequence. It differs from the earlier `periodic_chunk_repetition_aversion` (pruned), which only penalised a whole sequence built by repeating a chunk. Here a single recurring chunk anywhere counts.\n\n**Model:** It is the incumbent, `personal_complement_symmetry_aversion`, with one added feature and one shared weight (`psi`, prior Normal(0, 1.5)). The feature is the length of the longest repeat divided by half the sequence length, the longest a repeat can be. Everything else in the incumbent is unchanged.\n\n**What wasn't checked yet:**\n- **Convergence:** the one-chain test can't report R-hat, so the full fit's R-hat ≤ 1.05 and bulk ESS ≥ 100 requirements are still open.\n- **Fit reliability:** the test fit flagged 8.3% of trials with high Pareto k, above the 1% tolerance, so that ELPD estimate may be off. The full fit with more draws will show whether this goes away.\n- **Speed:** the 100-draw run took about 2 minutes. The full fit has to finish within 30 minutes or the candidate is rejected as too slow.\n- **Novelty:** the check doesn't test whether the model's predictions differ enough from existing models. If `psi` comes out near zero, it could be rejected as a near-duplicate of the incumbent.\n\nThe three files are in `/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_3/candidate_1/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2292,"cache_read_input_tokens":87729,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2292,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9283948b-301c-4a9c-b231-cc652b0a4cf7","uuid":"86335fa4-a062-4eb8-861a-a23cc88da2d7","timestamp":"2026-10-02T16:00:57.143Z","request_id":"req_011CfdgxPEZ97VtXUZsUai9Y"}
